      ],
      "text": "The architecture separates understanding from retrieval: the LLM judges what is worth remembering, extracts atomic facts, classifies scope/family/kind, and detects conflicts, while FTS5/BM25 handles retrieval, filtering, ranking, and top-K recall; embeddings are not relied on by default."
    },
